<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 27-day Cetes seen at 18.86 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 27-day Cetes seen at 18.86 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether one-month Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 60 basis points to 18.86 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of eight Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    27-DAY     19.46	    18.86		   - 60 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     21.29	    20.87		   - 42 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    22.60	    22.22		   - 38 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.40	    23.14		   - 26 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1930 EST.</p>
<p>((- Patricia Lezama, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289554))</p>
